# =====================================================================================
# ring.shapes.ttl — the RING rung's per-law SHACL tooth (W2 · SP0 · Stage 3a, T-RING).
# =====================================================================================
# The two-operation DISTRIBUTIVITY tooth of the ring rung, authored into its OWN per-rung shapes file
# (shapes/<rung>.shapes.ttl, the T-2OP-INFRA lockstep convention that keeps parallel rung executors off
# a shared shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl write race; run-algebra-checks.sh globs shapes/*.shapes.ttl and
# merges them into ONE shapes graph, so this tooth is loaded, validated and 0-focus-gated alongside the
# base spine teeth). It is the two-operation analogue of the one-operation per-law teeth
# (shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl SemigroupAssociativityShape / GroupInverseShape ...): a sh:sparql clause over
# the reified finite Cayley tables, sh:targetClass rec:model:record (NEVER sh:targetNode, the design §4
# anti-pattern the runner's 0-focus gate detects).
#
# WHAT IT CHECKS. Left distributivity x·(y+z) = x·y + x·z over a ring model's TWO reified Cayley tables
# (the additive + and multiplicative · rows, discriminated by @rel:operation:discriminator,
# records_twoop.ttl). For every triple (x,y,z) it forms x·(y+z) (an additive row y+z=s then a
# multiplicative row x·s=lhs) and x·y + x·z (two multiplicative rows then an additive row p+q=rhs) and
# reddens when lhs != rhs — the distributivity law FAILS. It re-homes fnd:RingDistribShape /
# q_ring_distrib (basicttl/foundation/algebra_rings.ttl:246-250,655) into the folded stratified idiom.
#
# TWO-TABLE / ONE-OP-TEETH ISOLATION. The one-operation per-law teeth walk `?cell @rel:structure <model>`
# with NO discriminator, so a ring's merged +/· rows scoped @rel:structure -> the model would let those
# teeth mix additive and multiplicative rows and falsely redden. The folded two-operation rows are
# therefore scoped @rel:structure -> a per-model REIFIED-TABLE node (linked from the model by
# @rel:reified:table, fixtures/ring_pos.ttl), keeping the discriminated rows OUT of the one-operation
# teeth's model-scoped scan (the T4/T5 isolation of algebra_rings.ttl:79, here via a distinct structure
# NODE). This tooth reaches the rows THROUGH the model's @rel:reified:table link, so its focus is still
# rec:model:record (data-graph focus = the ring model-record class, vacuous since it declares no
# @rel:reified:table; the finite GF(3) witness in fixtures/ is where it bites).
#
# RED->GREEN (design §4 fixture polarity). fixtures/ring_pos.ttl (GF(3)=Z/3, a genuine field-as-ring, every
# distributivity triple holds) conforms (0 rows). fixtures/ring_neg.ttl (the SAME GF(3) tables with the
# SINGLE multiplicative row 1·2 perturbed from 2 to 1) makes the triple (x,y,z)=(1,1,1) fail — x·(y+z) =
# 1·(1+1) = 1·2 = 1 while x·y + x·z = (1·1)+(1·1) = 1+1 = 2 — so >= 1 row and conforms True->False. The
# probe of record probes/ring_distributivity.rq is the executable SPARQL twin.
#
# Prefix labels follow the fold-tree convention (shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl:22-35): the SHACL namespace is
# labelled `constraint:` and record ladder `rec:` — same IRIs as sh:/rec:, so pyshacl is unaffected. Full
# runtime Linnaean-ladder IRIs (relation:*, the algebra discriminators) are written VERBATIM inside the
# sh:select string (SPARQL does not inherit the file's @prefix, exactly as the base spine teeth do).
#
# Design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-w2-sp0-primordial-fold-design.md (§4 per-law teeth, §6 fan-out).
# Folds FROM: basicttl/foundation/algebra_rings.ttl:246-250,655 (fnd:lawDistributivity / fnd:ringModel).

@prefix constraint:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix schema:      <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix relation:    <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:> .
# seed-carrier record-class ladder (records.ttl:38-39) — rec:model:record targeted:
@prefix rec:         <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:grounding:ontology:basic:formal:domain:knowledge:representation:kingdom:specification:phylum:formal:contract:class:class:order:declared:family:seed:genus:registry:species:> .

# =====================================================================================
# RingDistributivityShape — the ring rung's characteristic two-operation tooth (left distributivity
# x·(y+z) = x·y + x·z) over the reified GF(3) tables. sh:targetClass rec:model:record (NEVER
# sh:targetNode). The sh:sparql joins additive rows (@rel:operation:discriminator = the additive
# discriminator, records_twoop.ttl) for the sum y+z and the sum (x·y)+(x·z), and multiplicative rows
# (the multiplicative discriminator) for x·(y+z), x·y and x·z, all scoped @rel:structure -> the model's
# @rel:reified:table node, and reddens when x·(y+z) != x·y + x·z for some triple. Focus in the data graph
# = the ring model-record class (vacuous, no @rel:reified:table -> conforms); it bites on the finite GF(3)
# witnesses in fixtures/. Proven by injection: fixtures/ring_neg.ttl (1·2 perturbed) flips conforms
# True->False; fixtures/ring_pos.ttl stays GREEN.
# =====================================================================================
constraint:RingDistributivityShape a constraint:NodeShape ;
    constraint:targetClass rec:model:record ;
    constraint:sparql [
        a constraint:SPARQLConstraint ;
        constraint:message "Distributivity violation (ring): over the reified two-operation Cayley tables of this model, some triple has x·(y+z) != x·y + x·z — multiplication does NOT distribute over addition (re-homes fnd:RingDistribShape / q_ring_distrib, algebra_rings.ttl:246-250)." ;
        constraint:select """SELECT $this ?lhs ?rhs WHERE {
  $this <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:reified:table> ?t .
  ?add1 <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:structure> ?t ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:operation:discriminator> <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:domain:mathematics:realm:algebra:subdomain:semiring:kingdom:definition:phylum:specification:class:discriminator:order:enumeration:family:operation:genus:additive:species:discriminator:component:definition:instance:canonical> ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:first> ?y ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:second> ?z ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:result> ?s .
  ?mul1 <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:structure> ?t ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:operation:discriminator> <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:domain:mathematics:realm:algebra:subdomain:semiring:kingdom:definition:phylum:specification:class:discriminator:order:enumeration:family:operation:genus:multiplicative:species:discriminator:component:definition:instance:canonical> ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:first> ?x ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:second> ?s ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:result> ?lhs .
  ?mul2 <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:structure> ?t ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:operation:discriminator> <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:domain:mathematics:realm:algebra:subdomain:semiring:kingdom:definition:phylum:specification:class:discriminator:order:enumeration:family:operation:genus:multiplicative:species:discriminator:component:definition:instance:canonical> ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:first> ?x ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:second> ?y ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:result> ?p .
  ?mul3 <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:structure> ?t ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:operation:discriminator> <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:domain:mathematics:realm:algebra:subdomain:semiring:kingdom:definition:phylum:specification:class:discriminator:order:enumeration:family:operation:genus:multiplicative:species:discriminator:component:definition:instance:canonical> ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:first> ?x ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:second> ?z ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:result> ?q .
  ?add2 <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:structure> ?t ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:operation:discriminator> <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:domain:mathematics:realm:algebra:subdomain:semiring:kingdom:definition:phylum:specification:class:discriminator:order:enumeration:family:operation:genus:additive:species:discriminator:component:definition:instance:canonical> ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:first> ?p ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:second> ?q ;
        <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:category:result> ?rhs .
  FILTER(?lhs != ?rhs)
}""" ] ;
    schema:comment "The RingDistributivityShape is the added-law tooth of the RING rung (distributivity, · distributes over +) as a SHACL shape (design §4 'per-law teeth ... on a SHAPE not only a probe'), the two-operation analogue of the one-operation per-law teeth. It targets rec:model:record by sh:targetClass (never sh:targetNode, the design §4 anti-pattern the run-algebra-checks.sh 0-focus gate detects) so the ring model-record class (spine/ring.ttl, punned owl:Class + rec:model:record) is a counted data-graph focus and the finite GF(3) witnesses (fixtures/) are where it bites. The sh:sparql joins the reified two-operation Cayley rows of the model's @rel:reified:table node, selecting additive rows by the additive @rel:operation:discriminator (records_twoop.ttl) for the sum y+z=s and the sum (x·y)+(x·z)=rhs, and multiplicative rows by the multiplicative discriminator for x·(y+z)=lhs, x·y=p and x·z=q, and reddens when lhs != rhs — left distributivity FAILS for some triple. It reaches the rows THROUGH @rel:reified:table (not @rel:structure = model) precisely so the discriminated two-operation rows stay OUT of the one-operation per-law teeth's model-scoped `@rel:structure = model` scan, avoiding false cross-table reddening (the T4/T5 isolation of algebra_rings.ttl:79). fixtures/ring_pos.ttl (GF(3), every distributivity triple holds) conforms; fixtures/ring_neg.ttl (the single multiplicative row 1·2 perturbed 2->1, so the triple (1,1,1) reads x·(y+z)=1·2=1 while x·y+x·z=1+1=2) reddens — the True->False flip probes/ring_distributivity.rq records, now also on a dedicated SHACL shape. Re-homes fnd:RingDistribShape / q_ring_distrib (algebra_rings.ttl:246-250,655) as an intensional SHACL law-check (D25 no-regression: BOTH probe AND shape). The vacuously-satisfied focus (the ring model-record class, no @rel:reified:table) keeps the data graph GREEN; only a model naming a non-distributive pair of reified tables reddens." .
